WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.467
-You look fantastic.
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.734
I can't even -- I'm not
even sure if I can tell you

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.968
how much I enjoyed
your performance.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:11.534
You were mind-blowingly genius
in "Sweeney Todd."

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:14.067
Really unbelievable.
You were fantastic.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:16.133
-Thank you.
-And I know --

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:19.601
Not only the comedy was great,
but also your dramatic acting.

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.334
Your singing was beautiful.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.400
It made people cry,
including me.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.501
But you made me laugh.
But also the accent you --

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:27.767
-Thank you.

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.133
[British accent] Thank you.
Thank you very much.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:31.501
-Wow! That's what I'm talking
about. That's all I want.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.067
Now I get to hear
your real voice.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:35.434
Let's talk about this later.
I want to talk about the family.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:36.601
I want to know more about you.

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.567
I know -- How old is your son?

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.167
-[Normal voice]
Oh, he just turned 7,

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.000
which is crazy, bananas.
-Seven.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.167
-Seven. You know, seven.
It's a fun one. It's a fun age.

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.767
-Is he into Halloween?
-Super, super into Halloween.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:49.901
He wanted to be Marty McFly.
I mean, so good, right?

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:51.634
-I would love that.
-Me too.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.834
But nobody at school
knew who Marty McFly was?

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:56.567
I mean, come on. What are they
thinking, these 7-year-olds?

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.567
-They're not ready for
"Back to the Future" yet.

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:00.133
But get ready.
It's a great movie.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:02.067
-Right? Can't wait.
-They're going to love it.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:04.367
-I was going to be Doc. I was
very excited about the wig.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.667
-That would have been fantastic.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.334
-I know,
but then he changed his mind.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.300
Then he was gonna be, like,
a werewolf from "Goosebumps."

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.067
And then we finally
settled on Beetlejuice,

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.901
which I feel really good about.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:17.300
Classic.
-He loves "Beetlejuice"?

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.434
-Loves "Beetlejuice,"
but he also has

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:22.501
a really special love
for Michael Keaton.

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:23.634
-Yes!
-Right?

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.367
-That's a good --
That's a good guy to love.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.033
-I feel like
I'm raising him right.

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.601
He's very concerned about

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:30.734
what Michael Keaton is doing,
how he is.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:33.634
He wants to meet him very badly.

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.267
So, Michael Keaton,
if you're listening,

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.934
my son would like
to meet you someday.

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.968
-Oh, he's a great guy to meet.
-I mean, the best.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:41.167
-Oh, he's a great guy to meet.
Yeah, he's really fun. Wait.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.567
I love -- He just is interested
in the actor Michael Keaton?

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:46.234
-Yes. Because Michael Keaton
was also Batman.

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:47.767
So he's --
You know, Michael Keaton.

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.300
Batman. Beetlejuice.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.968
It's really, really, like,
an exciting time

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.934
in Michael Keaton's career.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:55.267
And so your son
has a Beetlejuice costume?

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.434
-Yes, yes.

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.701
He was very insistent
that there was also

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:02.367
some male pattern baldness
involved in the wig.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:03.834
It's good.
-Here's a sneak peek

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.701
of what you'll see
tomorrow on Halloween

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.067
walking the streets.
-Tomorrow! Yeah.

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:09.734
-Little guy running around.
-Look at that. Really good.

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:14.067
-Stop it. He is so cute.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.667
-So good. Yeah.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:18.067
Next year, he's gonna
be Birdman. It's great.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:21.801
-Oh. He's so cute. Now, you --

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:24.000
Were you a funny kid, too,
just like your son?

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.033
-Well, you know,
I liked funny things.

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:30.400
I loved --
I love "The Carol Burnett Show."

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.868
And I loved "Golden Girls"
and I loved "SNL."

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:34.634
I was a big, big "SNL" kid.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.501
I also --
I loved "The Tonight Show."

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.300
I used to watch it
with my grandpa.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.767
So this is like --
kind of like -- I had the feels.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.467
I was like,
"I'm making my debut!"

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:45.634
-Yes. You're making a debut.
Exactly.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.968
For grandpa.
-For my grandpa.

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:49.734
-We love you, Grandpa. Come on.
-I know.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.934
Also, why was he letting me
watch that late at night?

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.734
-And "Saturday Night Live, too."
-I know.

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:55.000
-I had those parents, as well.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.901
They would let me watch
"The Tonight Show."

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:58.634
I go, "Can I just stay up
to watch Johnny's monologue?"

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:01.501
-Uh! Me too! Yeah. The best.
And then I also was very,

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:03.567
very interested
in Barbra Streisand's skin

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:06.601
because I thought it --
it must be like "buttah."

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:08.234
It had to be like buttah.
-Oh, my gawsh.

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:09.868
-I was very into the --

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:11.100
-"Coffee Tawk."
"Coffee Tawk."

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.834
Very into "Coffee Talk."
And the Church Lady.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.734
Those were, like, my two bits
that I did at parties.

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:18.367
From the ages of like 4 to 7,
that was, like, my bit.

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:20.968
-You said that you're not
very good at taking headshots.

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:22.868
-No.
-And I go, "What do you mean?"

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.667
You go, "Well, I'll bring you
two just to show you examples."

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:27.400
Now, this is your
first headshot, right?

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.601
-Yeah.
This is, like, when I was 14,

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:31.133
but I look like a woman.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.734
I look like a weird woman.
Like, why?

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:35.267
-You were 14 years old?

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:37.467
-Yeah, I know I look older there
than I do now.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.100
It's very uncomfortable.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.334
-Wow. I mean, very glamorous.
-So much hair, too.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.968
I mean, big hair.
There's a lot going on.

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:46.534
And then there was just a series

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.167
of bad headshots
when I was a kid.

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:51.200
Like, this one summer --
You know when Sun-In came out?

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.567
-[ Gasps ]
-It was the thing.

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.167
It was the thing.
-I did Sun-In.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.267
-You did, too? It's so good.
-Yeah, my sister had it.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:58.033
And I was like,
"Well, let me just try it."

00:03:58.033 --> 00:03:59.434
And then it turns
your hair orange.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:01.968
-Oh, yeah.
Full-blown white for me.

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:04.868
I was like -- Ohh.
I was very platinum blond.

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.033
-[ Laughs ] "Ohh."

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.367
-It worked.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:09.234
-I like that character.
I was like, "Ohh!"

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.667
-"Ohh. I was so ohh.
I was like, "I'm going

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.934
to Lake Powell
and using my Sun-In. Ohh."

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:18.067
It was so, so much.
And it worked.

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:19.701
[ Applause ]

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.367
So that was, like, July.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:26.901
And then by October,
I had a full 3 inches of root,

00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:28.834
and it was time
to take my new headshots,

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.968
and this is what happened.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:32.968
[ Audience groans ]

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:35.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:36.567
-Come on. That's so cute.

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:38.534
-You hear that audience
reaction?

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:40.634
It's like,
"Oh. I'm sorry for you."

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.234
-Come on. That's so cute.

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:44.234
-I don't think
I've really ever shared this.

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:46.501
It's really -- This takes
a lot of balls to share.

00:04:46.501 --> 00:04:49.801
Also my eyebrows. I needed
to get my eyebrows plucked.

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:52.033
-What are you talking about?
You're adorable!

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:53.601
Are you kidding me?
-It's a lot.

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:55.400
-Well, look at this. This --

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.801
This kid grows up
to be in "Sweeney Todd."

00:04:57.801 --> 00:04:58.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:01.100
And crushing it.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.734
Amazing performance.

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:06.033
The story is pretty dark,

00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:07.767
but there are
a lot of funny parts.

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:09.934
And, again,
you going down the stairs --

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:12.434
There's this physical thing.
I'm not spoiling it

00:05:12.434 --> 00:05:15.501
because, if you can,
run and go see this because --

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.200
January 14th?
-You got it.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.834
-You're leaving.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:20.934
Me and Josh Groban. Sweet
Josh Groban. Who's brilliant.

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:23.133
-You're great together.
You're so great.

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:25.334
You're both going.
-We're both going. Yeah.

00:05:25.334 --> 00:05:27.567
-Are you -- Are you sad?
It is bittersweet?

00:05:27.567 --> 00:05:29.167
Or is it after you've done
250 performances,

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:30.834
you're like, "Yeah..."

00:05:30.834 --> 00:05:33.934
-I mean, it's been one of
the most humbling blessings

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.667
of my career,
getting to play this part.

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:39.701
I grew up loving Angela Lansbury
so much that I used to just say

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:41.267
I want to be her
when I grow up, you know?

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:43.501
And then I kind of got to be
for the last year.

00:05:43.501 --> 00:05:44.834
So it's been such a blessing.

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:47.200
But I'm, you know,
gonna miss it.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.968
-But Angela Lansbury,
Patti LuPone

00:05:48.968 --> 00:05:50.901
have done this role,
and now you...

00:05:50.901 --> 00:05:52.868
-Talk about those shoes.
-Yeah. I know.

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:54.834
Talk about those shoes to fill.

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:58.234
And you filled it very well,
by the way.

00:05:58.234 --> 00:06:01.601
You have a picture
that you took. You did "Wicked"?

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:02.868
-I did "Wicked" many moons ago.

00:06:02.868 --> 00:06:04.367
They're actually --
They're having

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:06.400
their 20th anniversary today.
Can you believe that?

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:09.033
All those witches! Yes.

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:13.834
I was -- I was a witch
many, many, many moons ago

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:17.133
when I was younger,
but on my last performance,

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:19.868
there's this incredible poster
of Angela Lansbury

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:21.901
when she did "Sweeney Todd"
at that same theater.

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:23.934
And I said -- [ Gasps ]
"I need to take a picture

00:06:23.934 --> 00:06:26.801
with Angela Lansbury, please,
please, as Mrs. Lovett."

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:29.601
And then we got this picture.
So that was like 18 years ago.

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:31.133
17 years ago.
-And look at you.

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:32.734
And now you're playing...
-That's me and Mrs. Lovett.

00:06:32.734 --> 00:06:34.701
-You're playing Mrs. Lovett.
-It's kind of bananas.

00:06:34.701 --> 00:06:37.634
-When you -- When you do --
When you play this role,

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:39.934
do you go like,
"I have a take on this,"

00:06:39.934 --> 00:06:43.634
or do you go,
"Can I be funny in this thing"?

00:06:43.634 --> 00:06:46.334
-No. You just pray. You pray.

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:47.834
-You pray. You go...
-You pray.

00:06:47.834 --> 00:06:49.868
And then you go to the script
and you say,

00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:51.968
"What does she want?
How is she going to get it?

00:06:51.968 --> 00:06:53.934
And who am I talking to?"

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:55.501
You know, you just go
to the basics.

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:59.234
And then all those years
of "Nick at Nite" and "SNL,"

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:00.567
they kind of seep in, too,

00:07:00.567 --> 00:07:02.167
and they just all
kind of meld together.

00:07:02.167 --> 00:07:03.634
You know. I don't know.

00:07:03.634 --> 00:07:06.534
-In the first maybe 10 seconds
that I'm watching you,

00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:09.167
you, like, fly --
flop into this thing, and I go,

00:07:09.167 --> 00:07:10.567
"Oh, my gosh!"

00:07:10.567 --> 00:07:12.667
Like, do you have bruises
and everything everywhere?

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:14.067
-Yes.
-You do?

00:07:14.067 --> 00:07:15.467
-They're all covered up
right now.

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:17.501
No. Yeah.
You know, I wear a shin guard.

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:20.801
I've got some really sensible
padding in my skirts.

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:23.767
But, you know, a good bruise
or two means you did it right.

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:25.701
-Oh, my God. No.

00:07:25.701 --> 00:07:27.567
But, I mean,
you're un-un-unbelievable.

00:07:27.567 --> 00:07:29.834
You have to.
You're gonna miss it, right?

00:07:29.834 --> 00:07:33.334
-Oh, of course. Yeah.
There's this incredible lyric

00:07:33.334 --> 00:07:35.367
in the show that, you know --

00:07:35.367 --> 00:07:38.300
Stephen Sondheim, one of the
greatest ever to have lived.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:41.167
He said, "Slow, love, slow.
Time's So fast.

00:07:41.167 --> 00:07:43.801
Now goes quickly.
See, now it's past.

00:07:43.801 --> 00:07:46.868
Soon will come. Soon will last.
Wait."

00:07:46.868 --> 00:07:48.767
And it means
just stay in the moment.

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:50.901
Because we're so blessed
to be here.

00:07:50.901 --> 00:07:54.567
-You are unbelievable, pal.
Come back whenever you want.

00:07:54.567 --> 00:07:56.434
-You're the best.
-You have to. I love you.

00:07:56.434 --> 00:07:58.133
Annaleigh Ashford.

00:07:58.133 --> 00:08:01.868
"Sweeney Todd" is now playing
at the Lunt-Fontanne Theatre.

00:08:01.868 --> 00:08:05.100
We'll be right back
with stand-up from Jesus Trejo.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.968
Stick around, everybody!

